{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"863581290645291018","content":"The full phrase now says \"Kill the damn murder goose.\"","created_at":"2021-07-14T07:58:24.568000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864777843006636063","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"M L","id":"290612027691368454","is_bot":0,"username":"mournfulleper"},"author_id":"290612027691368454","channel_id":"863581290645291018","content":"*I become lost in reverie, a kind of walking meditation that has taken me often since I first found myself on this dirty skiff. Time passes.*\n*I huddle in the coat and whisper my name, tasting it and trying it different ways. I organize piles of dirty rags, and broken furniture, and pigeons. I study the essence I found in the sewer, and try not to remember the horrible things I saw and did there. Explosions happen. Close by. Sometimes I am afraid. Sometimes I know I should be helping, but it is hard to remember who, and why. I feel guilty.*\nI look up blearily and Dolores is there. She is holding a goose feather in her beak and she has quite the disapproving look on her face.\n\"Yeesh.\" I say, embarrassed. \"How long has it been?\"\nShe cocks her head. \"Coo.\"\n\"You're right.\" I tell her. \"But how?\"\nI stand there for a moment, thinking. Idly I wave my hand and clean the grime from my body. Realizing how painfully hungry I am, I discover the most irritating craving for a Copper's sandwich.\nFor the first time in days, I shrug into my huge green overcoat and step out on to <#863362543585329162>.","created_at":"2021-07-16T00:52:31.540000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"865395441570938900","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
